In compliance with the procedures outlined in the Preliminary Report, the TCU forwarded this Commission, through Notice No. 380-Seses-TCU of June 1, 2017, a copy of Decision No. 1139/2017 issued by the Full Court of that court in the proceedings No. TC 036.037/2016-8, reported by Minister Weder de Oliveira during the Ordinary Session of May 31, 2017, accompanied by the Report and Vote that underpinned it, with the following excerpt:

**VIEWED, reported, and discussed these records of a request from the National Congress, prepared by the Committee on Financial Oversight and Control of the Chamber of Deputies (CFFC), for the Tribunal to oversee the use of funds transferred to the municipality of Tarauacá/AC in 2012 by the National Fund for Educational Development (FNDE), intended for the construction of preschools.**

**THE MINISTERS OF THE UNION ACCOUNTING COURT, meeting in plenary session,** based on the reasons presented by the rapporteur, **DECIDE:**

9.1. To inform the Committee on Financial Oversight and Control of the Chamber of Deputies that:

9.1.1. Only one of the two kindergartens/preschools that were to be built with resources from the PAC commitment term 202501/2012 was completed;

9.1.2. Although the construction work of the kindergarten/preschool identified in the Integrated Monitoring, Execution, and Control System (Simec) with the number 24270 has not even started, the municipality of Tarauacá/AC paid Construtora Vitória Com. e Rep. Ltda. the amount of R$ 218,396.85, in violation of Articles 62 and 63 of Law 4.320/1964;

9.1.3. The municipality of Tarauacá/AC did not require Construtora Vitória Com. e Rep. Ltda. to provide guarantees for the contract 69/2012, in violation of the provisions of Clause VIII of the price quotation tender 8/2012;

9.1.4. The Tribunal will convert this request into a special accounting inquiry;

9.2. To order the conversion of the records into a special accounting inquiry, in accordance with Article 47 of Law 8.443/1993;

9.3. To declare this request fully met, in accordance with Article 14, IV, of TCU Resolution 215/2008;

9.4. To inform this decision to the interested parties and responsible individuals.

The guiding vote of the above Decision succinctly describes the object and measures adopted by the oversight conducted by the TCU, within the scope of processo nº TC-036.037/2016-8, as follows:

This is a request from the National Congress, prepared by the Committee on Financial Oversight and Control of the Chamber of Deputies (CFFC), through Letter No. 251/2016/CFFC-P of December 13, 2016, in response to a proposal for oversight and control 80/2016, which requested the Tribunal to conduct oversight of the use of funds transferred to the municipality of Tarauacá/AC by the National Fund for Educational Development (FNDE) for the purpose of building preschools.

